      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Starting your garment finishing service with SDF Clothing follows a structured process designed to ensure your finishing requirements are understood and results meet expectations. The process begins with providing detailed specifications, after which we guide you through sample development and bulk processing.</p>
        
        <p>Step one is to submit your finishing requirements through our contact form or email. Essential information includes: garment type and quantity, label specifications (type, size, placement), packaging requirements, folding standards, quality criteria, and desired timeline. If you have label artwork or packaging designs, include them for clarity. For garments we manufacture, finishing specifications are coordinated with our production team.</p>
        
        <p>Step two involves our technical review and quotation. Within 24-48 hours of receiving your requirements, we provide a detailed quotation including finishing costs, label production costs, packaging costs, quality inspection, and any additional services. The quotation specifies lead times for sampling and bulk processing, minimum order quantities, and payment terms. For custom labels or packaging, we may provide separate quotations for material production. You may request revisions to the quotation to adjust specifications to meet budget targets.</p>
        
        <p>Step three is sample finishing and approval. After quotation acceptance, we proceed with sample development, typically taking 3-5 days for standard services and 5-7 days for complex combinations. Samples are shipped to you for review, and we provide detailed inspection reports documenting finishing results. You may approve samples as-is, request parameter adjustments, or proceed with additional sample rounds. Each sample round adds 2-3 days but ensures the final finishing meets your expectations. We recommend thorough sample approval before bulk processing.</p>
        
        <p>Step four is bulk finishing confirmation. Once finishing parameters are approved, we require a deposit to confirm processing and schedule production. Standard terms are 30% deposit with order confirmation and 70% before shipment. Processing begins after deposit receipt and garment receipt. We provide a processing schedule with key milestones including finishing completion, quality inspection, and expected delivery date. Throughout processing, we provide status updates on batch progress.</p>
        
        <p>Step five is final inspection and delivery. Before shipment, we conduct final quality inspection using our standard protocols with additional verification that finishing meets specifications. We provide an inspection report for your review. Once inspection is approved, we finalize packaging and prepare shipping documentation. Balance payment is required before release of finished garments. We provide all necessary documentation for your records and any regulatory requirements.</p>
        
        <p>Throughout the process, our team provides technical guidance on finishing optimization, label specifications, and packaging selection. We understand that finishing enhances both presentation and perceived value, requiring attention to detail and quality standards. Clear communication about your presentation requirements and quality expectations helps us deliver finished garments that enhance your brand and meet retail standards.</p>
